<title>RUSSIA: Russia 6-mth T-bill yield falls to 49.63 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 6-mth T-bill yield falls to 49.63 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 49.63 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 65.98 percent at the previous auction on October 2, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast an average yield in the 55-62 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the issue follow:  </p>
<p>				    Oct 9		   Oct 2</p>
<p>    Series number	     22053		   22052</p>
<p>    Issue volume		10.00 trln rbls     8.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million	 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    15.92 trln	   11.28 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     9.49 trln	    6.61 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     7.17 trln	    4.70 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     75.55 pct	    71.18 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   75.55 pct	    71.00 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     49.63 pct	    65.98 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  49.63 pct	    66.56 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 238 days	     224 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		  Oct 10, 1996	 Oct 2, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     June 4, 1997	 May 14, 1997</p>
<p>On October 9 the finance ministry will pay about 1.1 trillion roubles in a coupon payment on the 18-month OFZ interest-bearing bond (series 24005) maturing in July 1997 and about five trillion roubles in a maturing six-month T-bill (series 22028).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
